<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sir Harry Smith, 1st Baronet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1787–1860</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Harry Smith was a British army officer who served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peninsular-war">Peninsular War</a> and won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-aliwal">Battle of Aliwal</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a>. As Governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> from 1847 to 1852 he annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-kaffraria">British Kaffraria</a> between the Keiskamma and Kei rivers and proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">Sovereignty</a> in 1848. The costly Eighth Frontier War led to his recall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sir-harry-smith-1st-baronet.jpg" alt="Sir Harry Smith, 1st Baronet" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Harry_Smith,_Bt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
